Beautiful, this did exactly what it was supposed to, appreciate the help immensely. But we now have another problem which you mentioned at the end. While the words themselves now have spacing the "select" area does not. Check the image below.
You mentioned re-drawing the entire itemRect lower which might be needed here...I think, I'm gonna be honest with you, I have no idea what I'm talking about so take what I say with a bag of salt.
So the solution I'm after here is to give the exact same spacing to the "Selection rect" as we did with the item names. I tried changing the "this.itemrectfortext" line but this doesn't change the selection area, instead it shoots everything out of bounds. Does this mean that the line of code for this is located in another file? Like for example "rpg_windows.js" or maybe somewhere else?

I think you can modify the item rectangle by making modifications to y values in the function below (where I currently put -= X), but looking at your pic it's unclear to me if you'd need to modify where the highlight appears directly with setCursorRect or something, and I've no motivation to try and find out at the moment. Maybe someone else can help you.
Window_EquipSlot.prototype.itemRectForText = function(index) {
var rect = this.itemRect(index);
rect.x += this.textPadding();
rect.y -= X;
rect.width -= this.textPadding() * 2;
return rect;
};

